# Sprite Rendering Optimization

## Context
- When working with numerous sprites in a game scene
- When implementing animated or frequently updated visual elements
- When targeting mobile or low-power devices
- When scenes contain complex or layered sprite arrangements

## Requirements
- Use sprite sheets instead of individual image files
- Apply appropriate sprite compression and size optimization
- Implement sprite culling for off-screen elements
- Utilize sprite pooling for frequently created/destroyed objects
- Set appropriate sprite depths to minimize overdraw

